loader: each tree's loader resolves kb/markers relative to its own package root (EYEKB_ROOT = parents[1] of mcp_server/eyekb_core.py); neither loader has a cross-tree fallback, so the copy that is authoritative for a run is the copy inside the tree the service is started from
divergence can change a served answer: in the git tree: no (the two panels are present where the loader looks for them). in the data tree: not today (that tree's loader is an older revision that does not name them) but yes the moment that wiring is synced there — the two libraries would resolve to nothing, silently
